    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the code for the door at the end of Log Cabin?</summary><p><b>358429</b>. It is written on the piece of paper you pick up at the very end of the level, after the last puzzle is solved, and the six-digit keypad beside the door takes it.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the four-digit code on the laptop in Level 8?</summary><p><b>1746</b>. The laptop on the desk by the window shows 0000 when you open it; the recording sets it to 1746 and the display takes it. We read the seven-segment digits twice at high zoom because OCR tends to confuse 7 with 0 and 6 with 3 on that font.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How many stained glass pieces and tiles are there in Log Cabin?</summary><p>Two separate collections: eight stained glass pieces, which reach 8/8 at 3:22, and five coloured tiles, which reach 5/5 at 2:46. They feed the two last puzzles, not the door.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is behind the animal portraits in Log Cabin?</summary><p>A red safe with twelve paw-print buttons, green and red buttons underneath them, and a gold dial on the right. Solving the wall opens the compartment; the safe itself opens after the paw-print sequence from the desk drawer.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does Log Cabin have a timed puzzle?</summary><p>No. Nothing in Level 8 is on a clock. The longest single puzzle is the hexagonal glass panel in the last third, which took the recording about ninety seconds.</p></details>

